<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kapaya Nayaka</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1368</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kapaya <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayaka">Nayaka</a> of the Musunuri family was a former Kakatiya commander who, allied with the founders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a>, recaptured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warangal">Warangal</a> from the Tughluq governor around 1336. He ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telangana">Telangana</a> from Warangal and supported the rebellion that founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate</a>, but was later defeated and killed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anapota-nayaka">Anapota Nayaka</a> of the Recherla family.</p></div>
